# Your company profile stays out of git. The fictional example ships as
# company/profile.example.md, so the repo still shows what a finished one looks like.
# To keep your own profile in your own repo, make that repo private, then delete the next line.
company/profile.md

# Your api.data.gov key. Never commit this.
company/.env.local

# Your opportunity pipeline. Target agencies, teaming partners, and bid decisions are
# competitive information, and some of it belongs to other companies.
# To keep your pipeline in your own private repo, delete the next two lines.
pipeline/*
!pipeline/opportunity.template.md
!pipeline/README.md

# Your proposal drafts, including pricing narrative and partner material under NDA.
# To keep your drafts in your own private repo, delete the next two lines.
proposals/*
!proposals/README.md

# Your local opportunity database and anything derived from it. /sync builds data/sam.db
# from SAM.gov, so it holds the NAICS codes you track, the set-asides you can bid, the
# agencies you are watching, and the notices you looked at. That is your pipeline strategy
# and it is competitive information. It is rebuildable, so nothing is lost by leaving it out.
# To keep the database in your own private repo, delete the next two lines.
data/*
!data/README.md

# SQLite's own side files, and any export taken from the database.
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
sam-export.*

# The generated dashboard. /dashboard builds it from your own files, so it holds your live
# pipeline, your deadlines, your target agencies, and your partner names on one page.
# It is generated output and is never hand-edited, so nothing is lost by leaving it out of git.
# To keep the board in your own private repo, delete the next line.
/dashboard.html

# Local Claude Code overrides (created when you choose "always allow" in a prompt)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Secrets in any other form
.env
.env.*

# The key file's example, which holds no key, is tracked on purpose.
!company/.env.local.example

# Operating system clutter
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editor folders
.vscode/
.idea/

# Office lock files, in case you open a draft in Word
~$*
